{
  "module": "The transformer block",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "layers-hidden-states",
    "title": "Layers and hidden states",
    "summary": "The middle of a transformer is a stack of layers, and the n × d_model vectors passing between them are the hidden states.",
    "covers": ["hidden-states-layer"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "embeddings",
        "reason": "The first hidden states are the vectors the embedding step produces."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "training-basics",
        "reason": "Each layer has its own parameters, which training learns."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "a-stack",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Between the embedding step and the output, a transformer does not do one big computation. It is a "
            },
            {
              "text": "stack",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " of stages, each one a "
            },
            {
              "text": "layer",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", also called a "
            },
            {
              "text": "block",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A transformer stacks "
            },
            {
              "text": "L",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " of them, and each has "
            },
            {
              "text": "its own parameters",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 12)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "hidden-states",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "What passes from one layer to the next? A set of vectors, one for each token, each of length d_model: an "
            },
            {
              "text": "n × d_model",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " matrix."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "These are the "
            },
            {
              "text": "hidden states",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", also called "
            },
            {
              "text": "activations",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". They are called hidden because they are neither the input text nor the final answer, just the working representation in between."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 12)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "updated-every-layer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Every layer takes the hidden states in and gives updated hidden states out: one vector per token, "
            },
            {
              "text": "updated at every layer",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The first hidden states are the vectors the embedding step produced, and the last ones are what the output stage reads."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 12, 18)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "real-sizes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Real models, from the deck's figures:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "GPT-2 small: d_model = 768, 12 layers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "GPT-3 (175B): d_model = 12,288, 96 layers"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "For a text of n = 1,000 tokens in GPT-2 small, the hidden states hold 1,000 × 768 = 768,000 numbers at every layer."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 65)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "own-parameters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The layers have the same structure, but "
            },
            {
              "text": "not the same parameters",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". A model with 96 layers has 96 separate sets of layer parameters, each learned in training."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The lessons that follow open one layer up and show what is inside it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 12)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "What is a layer (or block) of a transformer?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "One repeated stage of the network. A transformer stacks L of them, each with its own parameters"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The hidden states pass through them one after another."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The list of tokens the model can read"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is the vocabulary."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "A single number the network learns"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is one parameter. A layer holds many."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "One token of the input text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Tokens are what flows through the layers."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
